{"name":"Plankton Green","hex":"#00534c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plankton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Organisms, especially small and microscopic ones, that drift in water.","A plankter, any single organism that drifts in water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plankton"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plankton","blocks":[{"text":"Plankton are organisms that drift in water but are unable to actively propel themselves against currents. Marine plankton include drifting organisms that inhabit the saltwater of oceans and the brackish waters of estuaries. Freshwater plankton are similar to marine plankton, but are found in lakes and rivers. An individual plankton organism in the plankton is called a plankter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Marine_microplankton.jpg/330px-Marine_microplankton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plankton","wikidata":"Q25367"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png/500px-Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png/500px-Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Global_ocean_chlorophyll_concentration_October_2019.png/500px-Global_ocean_chlorophyll_concentration_October_2019.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Global_ocean_chlorophyll_concentration_October_2019.png/500px-Global_ocean_chlorophyll_concentration_October_2019.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Ocean chlorophyll concentration is a proxy for, or an indicator of, the distribution and abundance of phytoplankton. The intensity of green indicates how abundant the phytoplankton are, while blue indicates where there are few phytoplankton. – NASA Earth Observatory, October 2019.[6]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlobal_ocean_chlorophyll_concentration_October_2019.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Emiliania_huxleyi.jpg/250px-Emiliania_huxleyi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Emiliania_huxleyi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Emiliania_huxleyi.jpg/250px-Emiliania_huxleyi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmiliania_huxleyi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Cwall99_lg.jpg/500px-Cwall99_lg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Cwall99_lg.jpg/500px-Cwall99_lg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACwall99_lg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Plankton_species_diversity.jpg/500px-Plankton_species_diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Plankton_species_diversity.jpg/500px-Plankton_species_diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Plankton species diversity Diverse assemblages of unicellular and multicellular organisms with different sizes, shapes, feeding strategies, ecological functions, life cycle characteristics, and environmental sensitivities.[16] Courtesy of Christian Sardet/CNRS/Tara expeditions","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlankton_species_diversity.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ocean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg/500px-Ocean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ocean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg/1280px-Ocean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ocean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg/500px-Ocean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea spray containing microorganisms in marine plankton can be swept high into the atmosphere and may travel the globe as aeroplankton before falling back to earth.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOcean_mist_and_spray_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Thaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg/500px-Thaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Thaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg/1280px-Thaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Thaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg/500px-Thaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A gastrotrich can lay resilient eggs capable of surviving years in a dry environment. Scale bar: 20 μm.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThaumastoderma_ramuliferum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg/500px-Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg/500px-Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont